#Scalability .
1)Read heavy optimization 
Since youtube is read-heavy , most traffic is handled by cdn and caches , reducing load on backend services.

2)Horizontal Scaling using Stateless services.
Horizontal Scaling means adding more servers so that the one server does not get overloaded by the traffic. “Horizontal scaling means increasing capacity by adding more server instances. In YouTube, backend 
services are stateless, so any request can be handled by any instance behind a load balancer. All state is stored in shared systems like Redis, databases, or object storage, which allows the system to scale 
easily and reliably.” Stateful means tied to one server.

3)Distributed Object storage
Videos are stored in Distributed object storage , and is replicated across various regions which ensures high durability and no single bottleneck.

4)Async Processing (like heavy computation)
Heavy work like video transcoding and thumnail generation is done by async processing. Done such that it can't block uploads. 
Video transcoding means converting a raw uploaded video into multiple formats and quality levels such that it can be streamed smoothly on different devices and network speed.

5)Chunking + Adaptive Bitrate Streaming.

#How availability is ensured ?
1)No single point of failure.
Multiple instances of each service exist behind load balancer. So, Load balancer routes traffic to another server , if one server fails.

2)CDN replication for video delivery.
CDN replication ensures video remains available even if individual CDN nodes fails.

3)Replicated video storage.
If one storage nodes fails , the another replica serves the video.
Object storage uses replication to ensure high availability and durability of videos.

4)Metadata availability using cache + db replicas.
Metadata cached in Redis . Database has replicas. If cache fails , fallback to database . If one DB replica fails , another replica serves data.

5)Graceful Degradation.
Even if something fails , video might load slightly slower. Lower quality may be served. But , system still works.























